abstract: The Hakai Institute Quadra Island Bioblitz (2024) was an intensive biodiversity
  survey of the marine and terrestrial habitats around Quadra Island, BC. Throughout
  the three-week BioBlitz, teams of taxonomists and field biologists made collections
  of specimens that were morphologically identified in the lab, photographed, and
  then processed for DNA barcoding, with the resulting sequence data added to the
  Barcode of Life Datasystem (BOLD). In addition to genetic analysis, a large number
  of additional species were documented using iNaturalist.
